(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m4"] = E["hr-m4"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-4-1"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-4-1-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-1","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Policies in plain English","tr":"Sade İngilizceyle politikalar","fa":"آیین‌نامه‌ها به زبان ساده"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can explain a contract term or a policy in plain English, and check that it was understood.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir sözleşme maddesini ya da şirket kuralını sade İngilizceyle açıklayıp anlaşıldığını kontrol edebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی یک بند قرارداد یا یک آیین‌نامه را به انگلیسی ساده توضیح بدهی و مطمئن شوی طرف مقابل فهمیده است."},"hook":{"en":"Explain each rule in plain words, then check it. A rule nobody understands will be broken. Page three made no sense to Deniz. Leyla said it again with four small rule words, and he understood.","tr":"Her kuralı sade kelimelerle açıkla, sonra anlaşıldığını kontrol et. Kimsenin anlamadığı bir kural çiğnenir. Üçüncü sayfa Deniz için anlamsızdı. Leyla aynı şeyi dört küçük kural kelimesiyle yeniden söyledi ve Deniz anladı.","fa":"هر قاعده را با کلمه‌های ساده توضیح بده و بعد کنترل کن. قاعده‌ای که کسی نمی‌فهمد، رعایت نمی‌شود. دنیز از صفحه‌ی سوم چیزی نفهمید. لیلا همان را با چهار کلمه‌ی کوچک قاعده دوباره گفت و دنیز فهمید."},"before":{"en":"Rewrite a legal-sounding rule in plain English for a new driver: who must do what, and when.","tr":"Hukuki dille yazılmış bir kuralı yeni bir şoför için sade İngilizceyle yeniden yaz: kim, neyi, ne zaman yapmalı.","fa":"یک قانونِ پر از زبان حقوقی را برای یک راننده‌ی تازه به انگلیسی ساده بازنویسی کن: چه کسی، چه کاری را، کی باید انجام دهد."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"5"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Say the rule the way a person talks","tr":"Kuralı insanların konuştuğu gibi söyle","fa":"قاعده را همان‌طور بگو که آدم‌ها حرف می‌زنند"},"body":{"en":"Legal words hide the action. Ask: who must do what, and when? Say that with \"you\" and short sentences. Then check with a real question, because \"Do you understand?\" usually gets a yes.","tr":"Hukuki kelimeler yapılacak işi gizler. Şunu sor: kim, neyi, ne zaman yapmalı? Bunu \"you\" ve kısa cümlelerle söyle. Sonra gerçek bir soruyla kontrol et, çünkü \"Anladın mı?\" sorusuna genelde evet denir.","fa":"کلمه‌های حقوقی کار اصلی را پنهان می‌کنند. بپرس: چه کسی، چه کاری را، کی باید انجام بدهد؟ همین را با «you» و جمله‌های کوتاه بگو. بعد با یک سؤال واقعی کنترل کن، چون جواب «فهمیدی؟» معمولاً بله است."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Rules in plain English: must, entitled to, if...","tr":"Sade İngilizceyle kurallar: must, entitled to, if...","fa":"قانون به زبان ساده: must، entitled to، if"},"steps":[{"en":"Required: must / need to + verb.","tr":"Zorunlu: must / need to + fiil.","fa":"برای کار اجباری، must یا need to و فعل ساده را به کار ببر.","ex":"You need to call your manager."},{"en":"Your right: be entitled to + noun.","tr":"Hakkın: be entitled to + isim.","fa":"برای حق تو، be entitled to و اسم را به کار ببر.","ex":"You are entitled to 30 days of paid leave."},{"en":"Forbidden: be not allowed to + verb.","tr":"Yasak: be not allowed to + fiil.","fa":"برای کار ممنوع، be not allowed to و فعل را به کار ببر.","ex":"You are not allowed to smoke in the trucks."},{"en":"A situation: If + present, then the rule.","tr":"Bir durum: If + present, ardından kural.","fa":"برای یک موقعیت، اول if با حال ساده را بیاور و بعد قانون را بگو.","ex":"If you are ill, call Omar before 7 a.m."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Meaning","Plain English"],"tr":["Anlam","Sade İngilizce"],"fa":["معنی","انگلیسی ساده"]},"rows":[["Required","You need to call your manager before 7 a.m."],["Your right","You are entitled to 30 days of paid leave."],["Forbidden","You are not allowed to smoke in the trucks."],["In this situation","If you are ill, call Omar before your shift."]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish 'hasta olursan' and Persian 'agar mariz shodi' sound future, so learners write 'If you will be ill'. English keeps if + present simple.","tr":"'Hasta olursan' gelecek gibi duyulduğu için 'If you will be ill' yazılabiliyor. İngilizcede if'ten sonra present simple kalır: If you are ill...","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «اگر مریض شدی» و حس آینده دارد؛ برای همین بعضی‌ها می‌نویسند «If you will be ill». در انگلیسی بعد از if حال ساده می‌آید: «⁨If you are ill...⁩»"},"wrong":"If you will be ill, call Omar before 7 a.m.","right":"If you are ill, call Omar before 7 a.m."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"In simple terms, ...","meaning":{"en":"Signals a plain-English version.","tr":"Sade bir anlatımın geleceğini gösterir.","fa":"خبر می‌دهد که نسخه‌ی ساده‌شده می‌آید."}},{"phrase":"If you're ill, you need to...","meaning":{"en":"States a rule for a situation.","tr":"Bir durum için kuralı söyler.","fa":"قانونِ یک موقعیت مشخص را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"Just to check, how would you...?","meaning":{"en":"Checks understanding without embarrassment.","tr":"Utandırmadan anlaşılıp anlaşılmadığını kontrol eder.","fa":"بدون اینکه طرف را خجالت‌زده کند، می‌سنجد که مطلب را فهمیده است یا نه."}},{"phrase":"plain English","meaning":{"en":"Simple, clear language without jargon.","tr":"sade İngilizce.","fa":"انگلیسی ساده و روشن، بدون اصطلاحات تخصصی"}},{"phrase":"contract","meaning":{"en":"A written legal agreement.","tr":"sözleşme.","fa":"قرارداد (توافق‌نامه‌ی حقوقی مکتوب)"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"The rules change by country","tr":"Kurallar ülkeye göre değişir","fa":"قانون در هر کشوری فرق می‌کند"},"body":{"en":"Probation rules depend on the country. In the UAE, under Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021, probation can last at most six months and cannot be extended. Turkey and the UK have their own rules and habits. Never copy a contract template from another country without a local legal check.","tr":"Deneme süresi kuralları ülkeye göre değişir. BAE'de 2021 tarihli 33 sayılı Federal Kanun Hükmünde Kararname'ye göre deneme süresi en fazla altı ay olabilir ve uzatılamaz. Türkiye'nin ve Birleşik Krallık'ın kendi kuralları ve alışkanlıkları vardır. Başka bir ülkenin sözleşme şablonunu yerel hukuki kontrol olmadan asla kopyalama.","fa":"قوانین دوره‌ی آزمایشی در هر کشور فرق می‌کند. در امارات، طبق فرمان‌قانون فدرال شماره‌ی ۳۳ مصوب ۲۰۲۱، دوره‌ی آزمایشی حداکثر شش ماه است و تمدید نمی‌شود. ترکیه و بریتانیا قوانین و عرف خودشان را دارند (در ایران هم قانون کار حدود خودش را تعیین کرده است). هیچ‌وقت نمونه‌قرارداد کشور دیگری را بدون بررسی یک مشاور حقوقی محلی کپی نکن."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از زبان حقوقی تا قاعده‌ی ساده"},"text":"Facts: The rule means: ask for leave before the leave starts.","item":"Staff shall submit leave requests prior to the commencement of the period concerned.","why":{"en":"Weak: legal words, and no clear action. Strong: you, the action, the time.","tr":"Zayıf: hukuki kelimeler var, net bir eylem yok. Güçlü: sen, eylem, zaman.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول پر از کلمه‌های حقوقی است و کار روشنی نمی‌گوید. نسخه‌ی دوم می‌گوید تو چه کاری را کی انجام می‌دهی."},"answer":"You need to ask for leave before it starts.","cut":["shall submit","prior to the commencement of the period concerned"],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap the legal words a new driver would never say.","tr":"Yeni bir şoförün asla söylemeyeceği hukuki kelimelere dokun.","fa":"روی کلمه‌های حقوقی‌ای بزن که یک راننده‌ی تازه هیچ‌وقت به زبان نمی‌آورد."}},"quick":{"prompt":"You want to use a UK contract template for staff in Dubai. What should you do first?","options":["Get a local legal check","Use it: contracts are the same everywhere","Just change the currency"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Get a local legal check: probation and other rules depend on the country. In the UAE, for example, probation lasts at most six months.","tr":"Yerel bir hukuki kontrol yaptır: Deneme süresi gibi kurallar ülkeye göre değişir. Örneğin BAE’de deneme süresi en fazla altı ay sürer.","fa":"اول یک بررسی حقوقی محلی بگیر: قانون‌هایی مثل دوره‌ی آزمایشی به کشور بستگی دارد. مثلاً در امارات دوره‌ی آزمایشی حداکثر شش ماه است."},"point":4},"remember":{"en":"Read your version aloud to a new driver in your head. Any word he would need a dictionary for? Swap it. Result of this lesson: you can explain a rule in plain English and check it. You also have a rewritten policy.","tr":"Kendi metnini aklında yeni bir sürücüye sesli oku. Sözlüğe bakması gereken bir kelime var mı? Değiştir. Bu dersin sonucu: bir kuralı sade İngilizceyle açıklayıp anlaşıldığını kontrol edebilirsin ve elinde yeniden yazılmış bir politika olur.","fa":"متن خودت را در ذهنت برای یک راننده‌ی تازه‌وارد بلند بخوان. کلمه‌ای هست که برایش دیکشنری لازم داشته باشد؟ عوضش کن. حالا می‌توانی قاعده‌ای را به انگلیسی ساده توضیح بدهی و کنترل کنی. یک آیین‌نامه‌ی بازنویسی‌شده هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Conditions: unless, provided that, as long as","tr":"Koşullar: unless, provided that, as long as","fa":"شرط‌ها: unless، provided that، as long as"},"steps":[{"en":"Only if: provided (that), as long as.","tr":"Yalnızca ... ise: provided (that), as long as.","fa":"برای «فقط اگر»، provided (that) یا as long as را به کار ببر.","ex":"You can swap shifts as long as your manager agrees."},{"en":"If not: unless, with a positive verb.","tr":"Eğer ... değilse: unless, olumlu fiille.","fa":"برای «اگر نه»، unless را با فعل مثبت به کار ببر.","ex":"Unless you call before 7 a.m., ..."},{"en":"Like if: present simple for the future.","tr":"if gibi: gelecek için present simple.","fa":"مثل if، برای آینده حال ساده می‌خواهند.","ex":"...provided you finish the route report."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Word","Meaning","Example"],"tr":["Sözcük","Anlam","Örnek"],"fa":["کلمه","معنی","مثال"]},"rows":[["as long as","only if","You can swap shifts as long as your manager agrees."],["provided (that)","only if (formal)","You may work from home provided you finish the route report."],["unless","if not","Unless you call, the day counts as unauthorised."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: your plain-English policy must include one sentence with unless and one with as long as or provided that.","tr":"B2 yolu: sade İngilizce politika metninde unless ile bir, as long as veya provided that ile bir cümle olmalı.","fa":"مسیر B2: متن ساده‌شده‌ی آیین‌نامه‌ی تو باید یک جمله با unless و یک جمله با as long as یا provided that داشته باشد."}},"source":{"en":"Probation facts from UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021.","tr":"Deneme süresi bilgileri BAE’nin 2021 tarihli ve 33 sayılı Federal Kanun Hükmünde Kararnamesi’nden alınmıştır.","fa":"اطلاعات دوره‌ی آزمایشی از فرمان-قانون فدرال شماره‌ی ۳۳ سال ۲۰۲۱ امارات."}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-4-1-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-1","title":"Rules in plain English: must, entitled to, if...","titleTr":"Sade İngilizceyle kurallar: must, entitled to, if...","exp":{"en":"Explaining a policy is mediation: you take dense legal text and say it simply. Use a small set of rule words. Must / need to = it is required: \"You need to call your manager.\" Be entitled to + noun = it is your right: \"You are entitled to 30 days of paid leave.\" May / can = it is allowed. Be not allowed to + verb = it is forbidden: \"You are not allowed to smoke in the trucks.\" For what happens in a situation, use the first conditional: If + present simple, then the rule: \"If you are ill, call Omar before 7 a.m.\" No will after if: not \"If you will be ill\". And entitled to takes a noun (\"to 30 days\"), while allowed to takes a verb (\"to take\").","tr":"Bir politikayı açıklamak bir aracılık görevidir: yoğun hukuki metni alıp basitçe söylersin. Az sayıda kural sözcüğü kullan. Must / need to = zorunlu: \"You need to call your manager.\" Be entitled to + isim = hakkın: \"You are entitled to 30 days of paid leave.\" May / can = izin var. Be not allowed to + fiil = yasak: \"You are not allowed to smoke in the trucks.\" Bir durumda ne olacağını anlatmak için first conditional kullan: If + present simple, ardından kural: \"If you are ill, call Omar before 7 a.m.\" If'ten sonra will yok: \"If you will be ill\" değil. Entitled to isim alır (\"to 30 days\"), allowed to ise fiil alır (\"to take\").","fa":"توضیح دادن یک آیین‌نامه نوعی «ترجمه» است: متن حقوقیِ سنگین را می‌گیری و آن را ساده می‌گویی. برای این کار فقط چند کلمه‌ی کلیدی لازم داری. must یا need to یعنی «لازم است»: «⁨You need to call your manager.⁩» be entitled to + اسم یعنی «حق شماست»: «⁨You are entitled to 30 days of paid leave.⁩» may یا can یعنی «مجاز است». be not allowed to + فعل یعنی «ممنوع است»: «⁨You are not allowed to smoke in the trucks.⁩» برای اینکه بگویی در یک موقعیت خاص چه باید کرد، از شرطی نوع اول استفاده کن: if + حال ساده و بعد خودِ قانون: «⁨If you are ill, call Omar before 7 a.m.⁩» بعد از if، will نمی‌آید: نه «If you will be ill». یک تفاوت ظریف هم هست: بعد از entitled to اسم می‌آید («to 30 days») و بعد از allowed to فعل («to take»)."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Meaning","Plain English"],"tr":["Anlam","Sade İngilizce"],"fa":["معنی","انگلیسی ساده"]},"rows":[["Required","You need to call your manager before 7 a.m."],["Your right","You are entitled to 30 days of paid leave."],["Forbidden","You are not allowed to smoke in the trucks."],["In this situation","If you are ill, call Omar before your shift."]]},"wrong":"If you will be ill, call your manager before 7 a.m.","right":"If you are ill, call your manager before 7 a.m.","blank":{"sentence":"If you ___ ill, call Omar before 7 a.m.","word":"are","distractors":["will be","would be"]},"wrong2":"You are not allowed smoke in the trucks.","right2":"You are not allowed to smoke in the trucks.","blank2":{"sentence":"You are ___ to 30 days of paid leave a year.","word":"entitled","distractors":["allowed","given"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Page three was fog to Deniz. Leyla said it again with four small rule words, and he understood.","tr":"Üçüncü sayfa Deniz için sis gibiydi. Leyla aynı şeyi dört küçük kural kelimesiyle yeniden söyledi ve Deniz anladı.","fa":"صفحه‌ی سه برای دنیز مثل مه بود. لیلا همان مطلب را با چهار کلمه‌ی ساده‌ی قانونی دوباره گفت و دنیز فهمید."},"tryWhy":{"en":"are: after if, use the present simple even for the future. No will after if.","tr":"are: if'ten sonra gelecek için bile present simple kullanılır. if'ten sonra will gelmez.","fa":"جواب are است: بعد از if حتی برای آینده حال ساده می‌آید و will نمی‌آید."},"rule":[{"en":"Required: must / need to + verb.","tr":"Zorunlu: must / need to + fiil.","fa":"برای کار اجباری، must یا need to و فعل ساده را به کار ببر.","ex":"You need to call your manager."},{"en":"Your right: be entitled to + noun.","tr":"Hakkın: be entitled to + isim.","fa":"برای حق تو، be entitled to و اسم را به کار ببر.","ex":"You are entitled to 30 days of paid leave."},{"en":"Forbidden: be not allowed to + verb.","tr":"Yasak: be not allowed to + fiil.","fa":"برای کار ممنوع، be not allowed to و فعل را به کار ببر.","ex":"You are not allowed to smoke in the trucks."},{"en":"A situation: If + present, then the rule.","tr":"Bir durum: If + present, ardından kural.","fa":"برای یک موقعیت، اول if با حال ساده را بیاور و بعد قانون را بگو.","ex":"If you are ill, call Omar before 7 a.m."}],"test":{"en":"Read your version aloud to a new driver in your head. Any word he would need a dictionary for? Swap it.","tr":"Kendi metnini aklında yeni bir sürücüye sesli oku. Sözlüğe bakması gereken bir kelime var mı? Değiştir.","fa":"متن خودت را در ذهنت برای یک راننده‌ی تازه‌وارد بلند بخوان. کلمه‌ای هست که برایش دیکشنری لازم داشته باشد؟ عوضش کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish 'hasta olursan' and Persian 'agar mariz shodi' sound future, so learners write 'If you will be ill'. English keeps if + present simple.","tr":"'Hasta olursan' gelecek gibi duyulduğu için 'If you will be ill' yazılabiliyor. İngilizcede if'ten sonra present simple kalır: If you are ill...","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «اگر مریض شدی» و حس آینده دارد؛ برای همین بعضی‌ها می‌نویسند «If you will be ill». در انگلیسی بعد از if حال ساده می‌آید: «⁨If you are ill...⁩»"}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["if you will be","if you will need","if you will call","if you will have","if you will not"],"fix":{"en":"No will after if: 'If you are ill, call your manager.'","tr":"if'ten sonra will gelmez: 'If you are ill, call your manager.'","fa":"بعد از if کلمه‌ی will نمی‌آید: «⁨If you are ill, call your manager.⁩»"}},{"find":["not allowed smoke","not allowed take","not allowed use","not allowed park","not allowed bring"],"fix":{"en":"allowed needs to before the verb: 'You are not allowed to smoke.'","tr":"allowed'dan sonra fiilin önüne to gelir: 'You are not allowed to smoke.'","fa":"بعد از allowed پیش از فعل to لازم است: «⁨You are not allowed to smoke.⁩»"}},{"find":["shall notify","prior to the commencement","failure to comply","per annum"],"fix":{"en":"This is still legal English. Say it the way you would say it to a new driver.","tr":"Bu hâlâ hukuk dili. Yeni bir sürücüye nasıl söylersen öyle yaz.","fa":"این هنوز زبان حقوقی است. همان‌طور بنویس که به یک راننده‌ی تازه‌وارد می‌گویی."}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-4-1-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-1","title":"Conditions: unless, provided that, as long as","titleTr":"Koşullar: unless, provided that, as long as","exp":{"en":"Policies often have conditions. Provided (that) and as long as mean \"only if\": \"You can swap shifts as long as your manager agrees.\" Unless means \"if not\": \"Unless you call before 7 a.m., the day will count as unauthorised absence.\" Because unless is already negative, do not add another negative: not \"Unless you don't call\". Like if, these words take the present simple for the future: \"provided you finish the report\", not \"provided you will finish\".","tr":"Politikalarda sık sık koşullar vardır. Provided (that) ve as long as \"sadece ... ise\" anlamına gelir: \"You can swap shifts as long as your manager agrees.\" Unless \"... değilse\" demektir: \"Unless you call before 7 a.m., the day will count as unauthorised absence.\" Unless zaten olumsuz olduğu için bir olumsuzluk daha ekleme: \"Unless you don't call\" değil. If gibi bu sözcükler de gelecek için present simple alır: \"provided you finish the report\", \"provided you will finish\" değil.","fa":"آیین‌نامه‌ها پر از شرط‌اند. provided (that) و as long as یعنی «به شرطی که» یا «فقط اگر»: «⁨You can swap shifts as long as your manager agrees.⁩» unless یعنی «مگر اینکه»: «⁨Unless you call before 7 a.m., the day will count as unauthorised absence.⁩» چون unless خودش معنای منفی دارد، یک منفی دیگر کنارش نگذار؛ نه «Unless you don't call». در فارسی هم می‌گوییم «مگر اینکه زنگ بزنید»، نه «مگر اینکه زنگ نزنید». این کلمه‌ها هم مثل if برای آینده حال ساده می‌گیرند: «provided you finish the report»، نه «provided you will finish»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Word","Meaning","Example"],"tr":["Sözcük","Anlam","Örnek"],"fa":["کلمه","معنی","مثال"]},"rows":[["as long as","only if","You can swap shifts as long as your manager agrees."],["provided (that)","only if (formal)","You may work from home provided you finish the route report."],["unless","if not","Unless you call, the day counts as unauthorised."]]},"wrong":"Unless you don't call before 7 a.m., the day will count as unauthorised absence.","right":"Unless you call before 7 a.m., the day will count as unauthorised absence.","blank":{"sentence":"You can swap shifts ___ your manager agrees.","word":"as long as","distractors":["unless","in case"]},"wrong2":"You may work from home provided you will finish the route report.","right2":"You may work from home provided you finish the route report.","blank2":{"sentence":"___ you call before 7 a.m., the day will count as unauthorised absence.","word":"Unless","distractors":["Provided","As long as"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: your plain-English policy must include one sentence with unless and one with as long as or provided that.","tr":"B2 yolu: sade İngilizce politika metninde unless ile bir, as long as veya provided that ile bir cümle olmalı.","fa":"مسیر B2: متن ساده‌شده‌ی آیین‌نامه‌ی تو باید یک جمله با unless و یک جمله با as long as یا provided that داشته باشد."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-4-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"You may leave early on Friday ___ all your deliveries are done.","options":["unless","as long as","in case"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"as long as: it sets a firm condition: only if the deliveries are done. 'Unless' means the opposite, and 'in case' is about being prepared.","tr":"as long as: kesin bir koşul koyar: yalnızca teslimatlar bittiyse. 'Unless' tersini söyler; 'in case' hazırlıklı olmakla ilgilidir.","fa":"as long as درست است، چون شرط قطعی می‌گذارد: فقط اگر تحویل‌ها تمام شده باشد. unless برعکس است و in case برای آماده بودن است."},"hint2":{"en":"Leaving early is allowed on one condition only. Which option means \"only if\"?","tr":"Erken çıkmak yalnızca tek bir koşulla serbest. Hangi seçenek \"yalnızca ... şartıyla\" anlamına gelir?","fa":"زود رفتن فقط با یک شرط مجاز است. کدام گزینه یعنی «فقط به این شرط که»؟"}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"Policies are full of conditions. Three phrases say 'only if' and one says 'if not'.","tr":"Yönetmelikler şartlarla doludur. Üç kalıp 'yalnızca ... ise' der, biri 'eğer ... değilse'.","fa":"آیین‌نامه‌ها پر از شرط‌اند. سه عبارت یعنی «فقط اگر» و یکی یعنی «اگر نه»."},"tryWhy":{"en":"Unless: it means 'if you do not call'. Provided and as long as would say the opposite.","tr":"Unless: 'aramazsan' demektir. Provided ve as long as tam tersini söylerdi.","fa":"جواب Unless است: یعنی «اگر زنگ نزنی». provided و as long as درست برعکسش را می‌گویند."},"rule":[{"en":"Only if: provided (that), as long as.","tr":"Yalnızca ... ise: provided (that), as long as.","fa":"برای «فقط اگر»، provided (that) یا as long as را به کار ببر.","ex":"You can swap shifts as long as your manager agrees."},{"en":"If not: unless, with a positive verb.","tr":"Eğer ... değilse: unless, olumlu fiille.","fa":"برای «اگر نه»، unless را با فعل مثبت به کار ببر.","ex":"Unless you call before 7 a.m., ..."},{"en":"Like if: present simple for the future.","tr":"if gibi: gelecek için present simple.","fa":"مثل if، برای آینده حال ساده می‌خواهند.","ex":"...provided you finish the route report."}],"test":{"en":"Replace unless with 'if... not'. If you now have two nots, delete one.","tr":"unless yerine 'if... not' koy. Şimdi iki olumsuzluk varsa birini sil.","fa":"به‌جای unless بگذار «if... not». اگر حالا دو تا منفی داری، یکی را پاک کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian magar inke and Turkish -mazsan already hold the negative, just like unless. Adding don't makes it a double negative.","tr":"Türkçedeki '-mazsan' (aramazsan) olumsuzluğu zaten taşır; unless de öyle. Yanına don't eklemek çift olumsuzluk yapar.","fa":"«مگر اینکه» در فارسی هم مثل unless خودش معنای منفی دارد. اگر don't اضافه کنی، جمله دو بار منفی می‌شود."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["unless you don't","unless you do not","unless they don't","unless he doesn't","unless she doesn't"],"fix":{"en":"unless already means 'if not': 'Unless you call before 7 a.m., ...'","tr":"unless zaten 'eğer ... değilse' demek: 'Unless you call before 7 a.m., ...'","fa":"unless خودش یعنی «اگر نه»: «Unless you call before 7 a.m., ...»"}},{"find":["provided you will","provided that you will","as long as you will","as long as he will"],"fix":{"en":"Use the present simple after provided and as long as: 'provided you finish the report'.","tr":"provided ve as long as'ten sonra present simple kullan: 'provided you finish the report'.","fa":"بعد از provided و as long as حال ساده بیاور: «provided you finish the report»."}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-4-1-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-1","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Contracts and Policies","tr":"Sözleşmeler ve Politikalar","fa":"قرارداد و آیین‌نامه‌ها"},"cards":[{"word":"contract","sentence":"Please read your contract before you sign it.","meaning":{"en":"A written legal agreement.","tr":"sözleşme.","fa":"قرارداد (توافق‌نامه‌ی حقوقی مکتوب)"}},{"word":"probation period","sentence":"Your probation period is six months.","meaning":{"en":"The first months of a job, when both sides check it works.","tr":"deneme süresi.","fa":"دوره‌ی آزمایشی (چند ماه اول کار که دو طرف می‌سنجند همکاری جواب می‌دهد یا نه)"}},{"word":"annual leave","sentence":"You have 30 days of annual leave a year.","meaning":{"en":"Paid holiday from work.","tr":"yıllık izin.","fa":"مرخصی سالانه (مرخصی استحقاقی با حقوق)"}},{"word":"sick leave","sentence":"Call your manager if you need sick leave.","meaning":{"en":"Time off work because you are ill.","tr":"hastalık izni.","fa":"مرخصی استعلاجی"}},{"word":"be entitled to","sentence":"You are entitled to one paid flight home a year.","gap":"are entitled to","accept":["are entitled to","be entitled to"],"meaning":{"en":"To have the right to something.","tr":"... hakkı olmak.","fa":"حق چیزی را داشتن؛ مشمول چیزی بودن"}},{"word":"policy","sentence":"Our sick-leave policy is on the intranet.","meaning":{"en":"A company's official rules about something.","tr":"politika, yönetmelik.","fa":"آیین‌نامه؛ خط‌مشی (قوانین رسمی شرکت درباره‌ی یک موضوع)"}},{"word":"plain English","sentence":"Can you say that in plain English?","meaning":{"en":"Simple, clear language without jargon.","tr":"sade İngilizce.","fa":"انگلیسی ساده و روشن، بدون اصطلاحات تخصصی"}},{"word":"per year","sentence":"Leave is 30 days per year (\"per annum\" in contracts).","meaning":{"en":"In each year.","tr":"yıllık, yılda.","fa":"در سال"}},{"word":"terms and conditions","sentence":"The terms and conditions are on page two.","meaning":{"en":"The rules of an agreement.","tr":"şartlar ve koşullar.","fa":"شرایط و ضوابط"}},{"word":"overtime","sentence":"Overtime is paid at 125% of your hourly rate.","meaning":{"en":"Extra hours worked after normal hours.","tr":"fazla mesai.","fa":"اضافه‌کاری"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-4-1-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-1","title":{"en":"Day One Words","tr":"İlk Günün Sözcükleri","fa":"کلمه‌های روز اول"},"text":"On the first of April, Deniz sat in a small office in the Dubai warehouse with a pen, a coffee and a twelve-page contract. Leyla was on the laptop screen from Istanbul.\n\n\"Take your time,\" she said. \"Tell me if anything is unclear.\"\n\nDeniz read slowly. Page three said: \"The Employee shall be entitled to annual leave of thirty (30) calendar days per annum upon successful completion of the probationary period.\"\n\nHe read it twice. He understood thirty. He understood days. The rest was fog.\n\nHe did not want to look stupid on his first morning, so he said, \"Yes, it's fine.\"\n\nLeyla had seen that face before, in the mirror, years ago. \"Can I tell you what page three says in simple words? I always need to.\"\n\nHe smiled with relief. \"Please.\"\n\n\"You get 30 days of paid holiday a year. Your first six months are a probation period: a test time for you and for us. After that, you can start using your holiday. And one more rule that isn't on page three: if you're ill, you need to call Omar before 7 a.m. Not a message to a friend. A call.\"\n\n\"Entitled,\" Deniz said. \"That means it's my right?\"\n\n\"Exactly.\"\n\nHasan, the dispatcher, walked past the door and laughed. \"I worked here two years before someone explained page three to me.\"\n\nThat afternoon Leyla wrote to the legal team: \"Could we add a one-page plain-English summary to every contract?\" She did not expect a quick yes. But she wanted to ask before the next new driver said \"Yes, it's fine\" to a page he could not read.","vocab":[{"word":"fog","en":"Here: something you cannot see or understand clearly.","tr":"sis, belirsizlik","fa":"ابهام؛ چیزی که روشن دیده یا فهمیده نمی‌شود"},{"word":"relief","en":"A good feeling when worry stops.","tr":"rahatlama","fa":"آسودگی خاطر؛ حس سبک شدن بعد از نگرانی"},{"word":"mirror","en":"Glass in which you see yourself.","tr":"ayna","fa":"آینه"},{"word":"dispatcher","en":"The person who sends drivers on their routes.","tr":"sevk sorumlusu","fa":"مسئول اعزام رانندگان"},{"word":"summary","en":"A short version with the main points.","tr":"özet","fa":"خلاصه"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why did Deniz say \"Yes, it's fine\"?","options":["He understood every word","He did not want to look stupid on day one","He had read the contract before"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct rule.","options":["If you will be ill, call Omar before 7 a.m.","If you are ill, call Omar before 7 a.m.","If you would be ill, call Omar before 7 a.m."],"correct":1},{"prompt":"What did Leyla ask the legal team for?","options":["A one-page plain-English summary for every contract","A shorter probation period","More holiday for Deniz"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Why did Leyla say \"I always need to\"?","options":["She did not understand the contract","To make it easy for Deniz to accept help without shame","She was joking about lawyers"],"correct":1}],"notice":{"en":"Deniz says 'Yes, it's fine' about page three. Watch how Leyla knows it is not fine, and what she does.","tr":"Deniz üçüncü sayfa için 'Yes, it's fine' diyor. Leyla'nın bunun böyle olmadığını nasıl anladığına ve ne yaptığına dikkat et.","fa":"دنیز درباره‌ی صفحه‌ی سه می‌گوید «Yes, it's fine». دقت کن لیلا از کجا می‌فهمد که این‌طور نیست و چه می‌کند."},"bridge":{"en":"'You get 30 days... If you're ill, you need to call Omar.' Next: see the four rule words behind plain English.","tr":"'You get 30 days... If you're ill, you need to call Omar.' Sırada: sade İngilizcenin arkasındaki dört kural kelimesini gör.","fa":"«⁨You get 30 days... If you're ill, you need to call Omar.⁩» قدم بعد: چهار کلمه‌ی قانونی پشت انگلیسی ساده را ببین."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-4-1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-1","topic":{"en":"Explaining Contract Terms Simply","tr":"Sözleşme Koşullarını Basitçe Açıklamak","fa":"توضیح ساده‌ی شرایط قرارداد"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of a form or contract you signed without fully understanding it. Which word was the problem?","tr":"Tam anlamadan imzaladığın bir form ya da sözleşmeyi düşün. Sorun hangi sözcükteydi?","fa":"فرم یا قراردادی را به یاد بیاور که بدون اینکه کامل بفهمی امضا کردی. مشکل از کدام کلمه بود؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Explain the probation period to Deniz in two simple sentences.","tr":"Deneme süresini Deniz'e iki basit cümleyle açıkla.","fa":"دوره‌ی آزمایشی را در دو جمله‌ی ساده برای دنیز توضیح بده."},{"en":"Explain annual leave: how many days, when he can start using them, and how to ask for them.","tr":"Yıllık izni açıkla: kaç gün, ne zaman kullanmaya başlayabilir ve nasıl talep eder.","fa":"مرخصی سالانه را توضیح بده: چند روز است، از کی می‌تواند از آن استفاده کند و چطور باید درخواست بدهد."},{"en":"Deniz asks: \"What if I'm sick on a Friday?\" Answer with an if-sentence.","tr":"Deniz soruyor: \"Cuma günü hastalanırsam ne olur?\" If'li bir cümleyle cevap ver.","fa":"دنیز می‌پرسد: «⁨What if I'm sick on a Friday?⁩» با یک جمله‌ی if جوابش را بده."}],"followups":[{"en":"Give the whole explanation in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"Açıklamanın tamamını 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede yap.","fa":"کل توضیح را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه بگو."},{"en":"Check he understood without asking \"Do you understand?\". Ask him to tell you how he would book a day off.","tr":"\"Anladın mı?\" diye sormadan anladığını kontrol et. Bir günlük izni nasıl alacağını sana anlatmasını iste.","fa":"بدون اینکه بپرسی «⁨Do you understand?⁩»، مطمئن شو که فهمیده است: از او بخواه بگوید برای گرفتن یک روز مرخصی چه کار می‌کند."},{"en":"Now explain one real rule at your workplace in plain English.","tr":"Şimdi iş yerindeki gerçek bir kuralı sade bir İngilizceyle açıkla.","fa":"حالا یک قانون واقعی محل کارت را با انگلیسی ساده توضیح بده."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"In simple terms, ...","meaning":{"en":"Signals a plain-English version.","tr":"Sade bir anlatımın geleceğini gösterir.","fa":"خبر می‌دهد که نسخه‌ی ساده‌شده می‌آید."}},{"phrase":"If you're ill, you need to...","meaning":{"en":"States a rule for a situation.","tr":"Bir durum için kuralı söyler.","fa":"قانونِ یک موقعیت مشخص را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"Just to check, how would you...?","meaning":{"en":"Checks understanding without embarrassment.","tr":"Utandırmadan anlaşılıp anlaşılmadığını kontrol eder.","fa":"بدون اینکه طرف را خجالت‌زده کند، می‌سنجد که مطلب را فهمیده است یا نه."}}],"culture":{"en":"Probation rules depend on the country. In the UAE, under Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021, probation can last at most six months and cannot be extended. Turkey and the UK have their own rules and habits. Never copy a contract template from another country without a local legal check.","tr":"Deneme süresi kuralları ülkeye göre değişir. BAE'de 2021 tarihli 33 sayılı Federal Kanun Hükmünde Kararname'ye göre deneme süresi en fazla altı ay olabilir ve uzatılamaz. Türkiye'nin ve Birleşik Krallık'ın kendi kuralları ve alışkanlıkları vardır. Başka bir ülkenin sözleşme şablonunu yerel hukuki kontrol olmadan asla kopyalama.","fa":"قوانین دوره‌ی آزمایشی در هر کشور فرق می‌کند. در امارات، طبق فرمان‌قانون فدرال شماره‌ی ۳۳ مصوب ۲۰۲۱، دوره‌ی آزمایشی حداکثر شش ماه است و تمدید نمی‌شود. ترکیه و بریتانیا قوانین و عرف خودشان را دارند (در ایران هم قانون کار حدود خودش را تعیین کرده است). هیچ‌وقت نمونه‌قرارداد کشور دیگری را بدون بررسی یک مشاور حقوقی محلی کپی نکن."},"model":"In simple terms, the first six months are a probation period. It is a test time for you and for us. You are entitled to 30 days of paid leave a year, and you can start using them after probation. If you want a day off, ask Omar two weeks before. If you're ill, you need to call him before 7 a.m. Just to check, how would you book a day off?","selfCheck":[{"en":"I explained probation in two simple sentences.","tr":"Deneme süresini iki basit cümleyle açıkladım.","fa":"دوره‌ی آزمایشی را در دو جمله‌ی ساده توضیح دادم."},{"en":"I used need to, entitled to or not allowed to correctly.","tr":"need to, entitled to ya da not allowed to'yu doğru kullandım.","fa":"need to، entitled to یا not allowed to را درست به کار بردم."},{"en":"My if-sentence had the present simple after if.","tr":"if cümlemde if'ten sonra present simple vardı.","fa":"در جمله‌ی شرطی‌ام بعد از if حال ساده آوردم."},{"en":"I checked understanding without 'Do you understand?'","tr":"Anlaşılıp anlaşılmadığını 'Do you understand?' demeden kontrol ettim.","fa":"بدون پرسیدن «⁨Do you understand?⁩» مطمئن شدم که فهمیده است."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-4-1-w","title":{"en":"A policy in plain English","tr":"Sade İngilizceyle bir politika","fa":"یک آیین‌نامه به زبان ساده"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-1","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Rewrite this policy paragraph in plain English for a new driver (40-70 words, short sentences, \"you\"): \"Employees shall notify their line manager of any absence due to sickness no later than one hour prior to the commencement of their scheduled shift. Failure to comply with this requirement may result in the absence being treated as unauthorised.\"","tr":"Bu politika paragrafını yeni bir sürücü için sade İngilizceyle yeniden yaz (40-70 kelime, kısa cümleler, \"you\"): \"Employees shall notify their line manager of any absence due to sickness no later than one hour prior to the commencement of their scheduled shift. Failure to comply with this requirement may result in the absence being treated as unauthorised.\"","fa":"این بند از آیین‌نامه را برای یک راننده‌ی تازه‌وارد به انگلیسی ساده بازنویسی کن (۴۰ تا ۷۰ کلمه، با جمله‌های کوتاه و با خطاب you): «⁨Employees shall notify their line manager of any absence due to sickness no later than one hour prior to the commencement of their scheduled shift. Failure to comply with this requirement may result in the absence being treated as unauthorised.⁩»"},"model":"If you are ill and cannot work, call your manager at least one hour before your shift starts. Please call: a message to a friend is not enough. If you do not call in time, the day may count as an unauthorised absence. This means an absence without permission, and it can cause problems with your record.","frame":"If you are ___, call ___ at least ___ before ___. Please ___: ___ is not enough. If you do not ___, the day may count as ___. This means ___.","words":[{"word":"if you"},{"word":"call"},{"word":"before"}],"minWords":40,"minSentences":4,"rubric":["Task done: who to tell, when, how, and what happens if not","Organised: the rule first, then the consequence","Language: if + present; need to / not allowed to; no legal words left unexplained","Tone: clear and friendly, not threatening"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: kime, ne zaman, nasıl haber verilir ve verilmezse ne olur","Düzen: önce kural, sonra sonucu","Dil: if + present; need to / not allowed to; açıklanmamış hukuki terim yok","Üslup: net ve samimi, tehditkâr değil"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: به چه کسی، کی و چطور خبر بدهند و اگر ندهند چه می‌شود","نظم: اول قانون، بعد پیامدش","زبان: if با حال ساده؛ need to / not allowed to؛ هیچ اصطلاح حقوقی بدون توضیح نماند","لحن: روشن و دوستانه، نه تهدیدآمیز"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"Who to tell, and how","tr":"Kime, nasıl haber verileceği","fa":"به چه کسی و چطور خبر بدهد"},"find":["call your manager","call","tell"],"sample":"call your manager; a message to a friend is not enough"},{"t":{"en":"When","tr":"Ne zaman","fa":"کی"},"find":["before","at least","hour"],"sample":"at least one hour before the shift"},{"t":{"en":"What happens if not","tr":"Yapılmazsa ne olacağı","fa":"اگر انجام ندهد چه می‌شود"},"find":["if you do not","unauthorised","may count"],"sample":"the day may count as an unauthorised absence"},{"t":{"en":"The legal word, explained","tr":"Açıklanan hukuki kelime","fa":"توضیح کلمه‌ی حقوقی"},"find":["this means","means"],"sample":"unauthorised = without permission"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-4-1-p","title":{"en":"Deniz on day one","tr":"İlk gününde Deniz","fa":"دنیز در روز اول"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-1","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Deniz on day one. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: which word in the contract confused you, and how did it feel to say \"Yes, it's fine\" when it wasn't?","tr":"İlk günündeki Deniz'sin. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: sözleşmedeki hangi sözcük kafanı karıştırdı ve öyle değilken \"Evet, sorun yok\" demek nasıl hissettirdi?","fa":"تو دنیز هستی، در روز اول کار. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: کدام کلمه‌ی قرارداد گیجت کرد، و وقتی همه‌چیز برایت روشن نبود، گفتن «Yes, it's fine» چه حسی داشت؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-4-1-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-1","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-4-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"If your truck ___ down, call the depot first.","options":["will break","breaks","would break"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"breaks: a real condition takes if + present. 'Will break' and 'would break' are wrong after if here.","tr":"breaks: gerçek bir koşul if + geniş zaman alır. Burada if'ten sonra 'will break' ve 'would break' yanlıştır.","fa":"breaks درست است، چون شرط واقعی با if و حال ساده می‌آید. will break و would break اینجا بعد از if غلط‌اند."}},{"from":"hr-4-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Part-time staff are ___ to sick pay.","options":["entitled","allowed","given"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"entitled: 'entitled to' means it is your right. 'Allowed to' is permission, and 'given to' doesn't make this meaning.","tr":"entitled: 'entitled to' bunun senin hakkın olduğu demektir. 'Allowed to' izindir; 'given to' bu anlamı vermez.","fa":"entitled درست است، چون entitled to یعنی حق توست. allowed to یعنی اجازه و given to این معنی را نمی‌دهد."},"hint2":{"en":"The gap is followed by to + a noun (sick pay). Which word means they have a right to something?","tr":"Boşluktan sonra to + isim (sick pay) geliyor. Hangi kelime bir şeye hakkı olmak anlamına gelir?","fa":"بعد از جای خالی ⁨to⁩ و یک اسم (⁨sick pay⁩) آمده. کدام کلمه یعنی حقِ داشتن چیزی؟"}},{"from":"hr-4-1","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is plain English?","options":["Leave shall be accrued per annum.","Entitlement is subject to accrual.","You get 30 days of holiday a year."],"correct":2,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'You get 30 days of holiday a year' says the rule the way a person talks. 'Shall be accrued' and 'subject to accrual' are legal language.","tr":"'You get 30 days of holiday a year' kuralı bir insanın konuştuğu gibi söyler. 'Shall be accrued' ve 'subject to accrual' hukuk dilidir.","fa":"«You get 30 days of holiday a year» قاعده را همان‌طور می‌گوید که آدم حرف می‌زند. shall be accrued و subject to accrual زبان حقوقی‌اند."}},{"from":"hr-3-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"A decision ___ been made.","options":["has","have","is"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"has: 'a decision' is singular, so has been + past participle. 'Have' is plural, and 'is been' is not English.","tr":"has: 'a decision' tekildir, bu yüzden has been + üçüncü hâl. 'Have' çoğuldur; 'is been' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"has درست است، چون a decision مفرد است و has been و اسم مفعول می‌آید. have جمع است و is been انگلیسی نیست."}},{"from":"hr-3-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"What exactly ___ you do?","options":["have","did","were"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"did: a past question about an action takes did + plain verb. 'Have' needs a past participle, and 'were' doesn't go with do.","tr":"did: bir eylemle ilgili geçmiş zaman sorusu did + yalın fiil alır. 'Have' üçüncü hâl ister; 'were' do ile gelmez.","fa":"did درست است، چون سؤال گذشته درباره‌ی یک کار did و فعل ساده می‌خواهد. have اسم مفعول لازم دارد و were با do نمی‌آید."},"hint2":{"en":"This asks about one finished event in the past. Which helping verb does the past simple use in questions?","tr":"Bu soru geçmişte bitmiş tek bir olayı soruyor. Geçmiş zamanda sorular hangi yardımcı fiille kurulur?","fa":"این سؤال درباره‌ی یک اتفاق تمام‌شده در گذشته است. در زمان گذشته‌ی ساده، سؤال با کدام فعل کمکی ساخته می‌شود؟"}},{"from":"hr-2-2","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which job ad line is free of bias?","options":["Young team seeks energetic men.","You will lift boxes up to 20 kg.","Native speakers only."],"correct":1,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'You will lift boxes up to 20 kg' describes the job, not the person. The other two exclude people by age, sex or origin.","tr":"'You will lift boxes up to 20 kg' kişiyi değil, işi anlatır. Diğer ikisi insanları yaş, cinsiyet ya da kökene göre dışlar.","fa":"«You will lift boxes up to 20 kg» خود کار را توصیف می‌کند، نه آدم را. دو گزینه‌ی دیگر آدم‌ها را بر اساس سن، جنسیت یا ملیت کنار می‌گذارند."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
